REGENT OF KARANGANYAR
CENTRAL JAVA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF KARANGANYAR REGENCY
NUMBER 3 OF 2017
CONCERNING
PROTECTION AND EMPOWERMENT OF WOMEN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF KARANGANYAR,
Considering : a. that women as an asset of the nation who play a role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations need to obtain guarantees for the fulfillment of their rights and Protection from acts of violence and Discrimination;
b. that in the context of Protection and means of self-actualization of women in society in Karanganyar Regency, there is a need for a Regional Regulation governing the Protection and Empowerment of Women;
c. that Regional Regulation of Karanganyar Regency Number 20 of 2009 concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children is deemed no longer in accordance with legal developments and community needs, so that a new regional regulation needs to be established;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection and Empowerment of Women;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) and Article 28I of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within Central Java Province;
3. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1974 Number 1);
4. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention The Elimination Of All Forms Of Discrimination Againts Women) State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
5. Law Number 13 of 1998 concerning Elderly Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1998 Number 190, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3796);
6. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention No. 138 Concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (ILO Convention Concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
7. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
8. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);
9. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
10. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
11. Law Number 23 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 58 Year 2007, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
12. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
13. Law Number 19 of 2011 concerning Ratification of the Convention On The Rights Of Persons With Disabilities (Convention Concerning the Rights of Persons with Disabilities), (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 107, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5251);
